Package: ggseqplot
Title: Render Sequence Plots using 'ggplot2'
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
  person("Marcel", "Raab", , "marcel.raab@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
         comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3097-1591"))
Description: A set of wrapper functions that reproduces most of the
  sequence plots rendered with TraMineR::seqplot() and several related
  plots from 'TraMineR' and 'TraMineRextras' (Gabadinho et al. 2011,
  <doi:10.18637/jss.v040.i04>). Whereas 'TraMineR' uses base 'R' graphics
  to produce the plots, this library draws on 'ggplot2'. The plots are
  produced on the basis of state sequence objects defined with
  TraMineR::seqdef() and, for some functions, event sequence objects or
  regression trees of sequences. The package automates the reshaping and
  plotting of sequence data. Resulting plots are of class 'ggplot', i.e.,
  components can be added and tweaked using '+' and regular 'ggplot2'
  functions.
URL: https://maraab23.github.io/ggseqplot/,
        https://github.com/maraab23/ggseqplot
